    "Cluster 2 — \"Older Adults with Diabetic-Range Glucose\" (699 patients): Average age 61, average glucose 204.3 within the clinically diabetic range (126+ mg/dL). This group has the highest rates of hypertension (25.1%) and heart disease (15.8%), and the highest stroke rate by far at 13.5%, nearly 3x the overall dataset average.\n"
